# Checklists (`ChecklistSection`)

Use `<ChecklistSection>` for tick-off resolution / workflow checklists — never hand-roll checkbox `ListRow` stacks.

```tsx
import { ChecklistSection } from '@/components/common/ChecklistSection';

<ChecklistSection
  title="Resolution checklist"
  items={checklist}
  onToggle={toggleChecklistItem}
  readOnly={false}
  actions={<Button variant="outline" size="sm">Add item</Button>}
/>
```

## Done-state visuals (required)

Checked items must show **three** cues — not the checkbox alone:

1. Checkbox `checked`
2. Label: `text-muted-foreground line-through` — use `CHECKLIST_DONE_LABEL_CLASS` from `ChecklistSection.tsx` if styling outside the component
3. Row: `opacity-80` on the `ListRow`

`ChecklistSection` applies this automatically. Do not build checklist rows without strikethrough + muted label when done.

## Data & actions

- Toggle: `toggleChecklistItem(id, done)` in demo/API layer
- Add item: `<SubEntityFormDialog>` + `createChecklistItem({ caseId, label, required })`
- Overview tab preview: same component with `readOnly` — checkboxes visible, not editable

## ListRow rules

- Always `leadingIsInteractive` so the checkbox does not steal row clicks
- Required items: trailing `<Badge variant="warning">` when open, `outline` when done
- Meta: `${done}/${total} done` — auto on `ChecklistSection` unless `meta` overridden

## Don't

- Raw `<Checkbox>` + `<ListRow title={string}>` without done label styling
- StatusBadge for checklist items — that pattern is for **Tasks** (Pending/Active/Completed), not tick-off checklists
- Inline add form — use `SubEntityFormDialog`

Reference: `/showcase` → Patterns → ChecklistSection · `/cases/:id` → Workflow tab
